Eco - the study of how living organisms interact with each other and with
non-living things.

Ecosystem.

Components of ecosystems:
	> Biotic - living part of the ecosystem.
		> Fungi, Plants,  Animals, Protists, Archare, Bacteria
	> Abiotic - non-living part of the ecosystem.
		> Soil, Light, Water
	

Biotic Factors: 
	Producers - grasses, trees, algae.
	Consumers - humans, frogs, tiger.
	Decomposers - worm, fungi, bacteria.

Energy Pyramid:
	> Producers - plants
	> Primary consumers - herbivores
	> Secondary consumers - semi-carnivores
	> Tertiary consumers - main-carnivores

Energy Transfer: 
	> the 10% rule.
	> the 90% is for the organisms growth.

Biodiversity - refers specifically to the variety of life
within that ecosystem, encompassing the range of species,
genetic diversity, and the complex interactions that occur
among them.

Ecosystem and Biodiversity is connected but not the same.

